    {
      "id": "hottake-not-photo-people",
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Not photo people? — directing camera-shy couples",
      "pillar": "Educational",
      "platform": "Instagram Feed",
      "status": "Published",
      "post_at": "2026-11-12T10:04:00Z",
      "published_at": "2026-11-12",
      "blog": "/blog/not-photo-people-camera-shy-couples.html",
      "caption": "\"We're not really photo people.\" We hear it on every first call — and honestly? Good.\n\nThe couples who think they're awkward end up with the realest photos. The stiffness isn't you, it's being told to \"just act natural\" while someone points a lens at your face. So we don't pose you. We give you something to do and someone to look at, and we disappear. The first ten minutes feel weird for everyone. Then you forget we're there — and that's where the good ones live.\n\nYou don't have to be photogenic. You just have to show up. How we direct camera-shy couples — full post on the journal, link in bio.",
      "tags": "#notphotopeople #camerashy #candidweddingphotography #unposedwedding #vancouverweddingphotographer #documentaryweddingphotography #bcwedding #yvrwedding #engagedvancouver #vancouverbride #realmoments #simplywedstudio",
